    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">30 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Creational pattern</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Asked at Amazon, Uber, PhonePe</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Abstract Factory</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Learn how one factory object can hand out a whole matching set of objects (a \"family\"), so your code can switch from one vendor, theme or platform to another by changing a single line, and can never mix parts from two families by mistake.</p>\n"
